    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0319" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.0012/616a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-14">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 14, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Eighteen peace treaties ratified yesterday. Is French Government disposed to
                    consider signing treaty agreed upon when Great Britain is ready or must it await
                    the conclusion of the war? It seems desirable that it should be signed as soon
                    as possible in order that both countries may have the benefit of it in case any
                    dispute should arise as result of the war. Has any answer been made to our
                    representations in regard to interpretation of section relating to report?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
